# candidate T28 -- the carrier decomposition computed ONCE
#   w-hat = G^-1(a . raw) is what v = D w-hat needs AND the response's
#   carrier slot. Both computed it, and chain_open recomputed v, so the
#   honest prover paid for it three times at the pin.
#   honest_compute_v_from_decomp is new (= mat_vec_mul);
#   honest_compute_resp_from_raw_32 and chain_open now TAKE it. None of
#   the three carries a criterion row or appears in a define_cases body,
#   so all three changed IN PLACE -- no _alongside duplication.
# This run is a GUARD, not a speed claim. T28's win is that an item is
#   called once instead of three times; criterion measures the item, so
#   no row can show it. quadeval/carrier_from_raw is unchanged code and
#   must read the same. Nothing may read slower.
# The win, measured on the pin profile instead (logs/runs/pin-profile-
#   20260918-{t29,t28b}.log, both exit 0, chain_verify = true):
#   honest_compute_resp + stack 338.7 -> 240.2 s, -98.5 s, -29.1%;
#   prover 1282.3 -> 1186.7 s, -7.5%; peak VmHWM 8477 -> 5453 MiB,
#   -3024 MiB, -35.7%. The R^lin assembly also fell 1.8 s -> 407 ms,
#   because the freed message pages are reused instead of faulted in.
#   Control for the phase read: the commitment stage, which T28 does
#   not touch, read +1.0% between the two runs.
